{"sections":[{"slug":"层上同调","section":{"metadata":{"slug":{"Plain":"层上同调"},"ext":{"Plain":"md"},"title":{"Plain":"(Abel) <span lang=\"zh\">层上同调</span>"},"taxon":{"Plain":"<span lang=\"zh\">百科</span>. "},"author":{"Lazy":[{"Local":{"url":"/SimplicialCat","text":"SimplicialCat"}}]},"page-title":{"Plain":"(Abel) 层上同调"},"data-taxon":{"Plain":"百科"}},"content":{"Lazy":[{"Plain":"\n<blockquote>\n<p>Before arriving at the full picture of higher topos theory … people had a pretty good guess about some aspects of this story, and this aspect they called sheaf cohomology. It turns out that sheaf cohomology is precisely the <em>abelian</em> part of general cohomology.</p>\n<p>Here is what “abelian part of general cohomology” means:\nFor many sheaves that appear in practice, the topological space $X(U)$ assigned to any test space $U$ is not just a topological space, but happens to have the structure of an <strong>abelian group</strong>, too. In this case a cascade of simplifications kicks in: first of all, such topological spaces, by a special case of something called the <strong>homotopy hypothesis</strong> (which is now really a precise theorem) can be identified with simplicial abelian groups. Second, by another theorem called the <strong>Dold–Kan correspondence</strong>, simplicial abelian groups are equivalently encoded more simply in the collection of data given by (non-positively graded) <strong>chain complexes in abelian groups</strong>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h2><span lang=\"zh\">定义</span></h2>\n<p><span lang=\"zh\">拓扑空间</span> $X$ <span lang=\"zh\">上</span> Abel <span lang=\"zh\">群层的上同调</span> $H^i(X,-)$ <span lang=\"zh\">是</span>"},{"Local":{"url":"/整体截面","text":"<span lang=\"zh\">整体截面</span>"}},{"Plain":" $\\Gamma$ <span lang=\"zh\">的右</span>"},{"Local":{"url":"/导出函子","text":"<span lang=\"zh\">导出函子</span>"}},{"Plain":", <span lang=\"zh\">也即</span> $X\\to *$ <span lang=\"zh\">的</span>"},{"Local":{"url":"/导出前推","text":"<span lang=\"zh\">导出前推</span>"}},{"Plain":".</p>\n<p><span lang=\"zh\">空间</span> $X$ <span lang=\"zh\">上的层上同调可视为</span> $X$ <span lang=\"zh\">上的</span> "},{"Local":{"url":"/∞-层∞-意象","text":"∞-<span lang=\"zh\">层</span> ∞-<span lang=\"zh\">意象</span>"}},{"Plain":"<span lang=\"zh\">中的映射同伦类</span>:\n$$\r\nH^n(X,F)\\simeq \\pi_0\\operatorname{Hom}_{\\operatorname{Sh}(X,\\infty \\mathsf {Grpd})}(X,B^nF).\r\n$$</p>\n<p><span lang=\"zh\">具体地</span>, <span lang=\"zh\">设有</span>"},{"Local":{"url":"/内射消解","text":"<span lang=\"zh\">内射消解</span>"}},{"Plain":" $F\\to I^\\bullet$, <span lang=\"zh\">定义</span> $H^n(X,F) := H^n(\\Gamma(X,I^\\bullet))$.</p>\n<h2><span lang=\"zh\">例</span></h2>\n<h2><span lang=\"zh\">相关概念</span></h2>\n<p>"},{"Local":{"url":"/Čech上同调","text":"Čech <span lang=\"zh\">上同调</span>"}},{"Plain":", "},{"Local":{"url":"/奇异上同调","text":"<span lang=\"zh\">奇异上同调</span>"}},{"Plain":".</p>\n"}]}}}]}